#### Alternative solution

Instead of expanding `BlockValidationResult` one could wrap the return value of `TestBlockValidity()` with `util::Expected` since it's the only function that returns this error. On the other hand, `BlockValidationState` is already quite diverse in it's various states. Not sure which one is preferable, I lean towards to the current PR approach.

