comments.body:
nit: Rather than having postconditions for the function, it seems slightly better to have preconditions upon entering, and separate them so it's easier to pinpoint failures:
```suggestion
        Assume(result != Result{});
        Assume(!reject_reason.empty());
        m_result = result;
        m_reject_reason = reject_reason;
        m_debug_message = debug_message;
        if (m_mode != ModeState::M_ERROR) m_mode = ModeState::M_INVALID;
```

Saw `inconclusive-not-best-prevblk` is covered in 2 functional tests. Not sure if it would add anything to also have a unit test covering the enum.

